WORK:
1. EXTERNAL PARTY PACK schema (src/vtt/party-pack.ts + JSON schema doc): a versioned, validated file format describing a 3-5 PC party in ENGINE VOCABULARY ONLY — SRD-describable classes/levels/abilities/AC/HP/speeds/attacks/spell selections by manifest spell id, conditions/effects by our typed ids. Loader validates deeply; every field outside the engine vocabulary is a typed refusal.
2. GAP REPORT emission (src/vtt/srd-gap-report.ts): when a party-pack feature fails to map, the loader emits a structured GapReport {packEntry, featurePath, requestedCapability, engineRefusalReason} — collected, never silently dropped (a pack with gaps loads its mappable subset ONLY if the pack declares allowPartial, else refuses whole). At play time: an ADJUDICATED event whose subject is not an engine-vocabulary id also emits a GapReport into the session's replay bundle (typed field, D317.11 schema extension within the migration window discipline).
3. SOAK RUNNER (tools/vtt-soak.ts, npm script vtt:soak): headless N-table runner: each table = coordinator + fake-or-real bridge config + partySource 'reference' | {packFile} alternating 50/50 by table index (D318.1), seeded, bounded rounds, writing replay bundles + a gap-report summary JSON per run to a --out directory. No network beyond the local bridge; real-bridge mode is config only (not exercised in tests).
4. partySource 'private' refusal from increment 9 becomes: 'external-pack' with the loader path — rename/migrate honestly.

GATE: loader property tests (valid pack loads; out-of-vocabulary feature -> typed refusal + GapReport; allowPartial semantics), soak runner smoke (2 tables, seeded, fake bridge, bundles + gap summary written and replayable), all authorized suites green, sim unchanged-green, tsc clean.

